  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2024-25, the Kiribati Australia Infrastructure (Te KAI) program supported the jobs of 46 I-Kiribati citizens, through the construction of the Kiribati Police Service (KPS) barracks and the upgrade of the Ministry of Infrastructure and Sustainable Energy&apos;s (MISE) headquarters. The KPS barracks project engaged two local contractors; KiriCraft (which prefabricated the structure) employed 10 men and 4 women, and Squareline (construction contractor) employed 20 men and 1 women. Importantly, these positions provided these local employees exposure to new building methods, and an opportunity to develop new skills. The MISE headquarters renovation created jobs for 8 men and 3 women. Senior staff within MISE remarked that the works on the headquarters &quot;set a new standard&quot; for Kiribati. Te KAI&apos;s projects are demonstrating the potential of locally led development, delivering quality infrastructure while building capacity in the construction industry.</narrative>
    </description>
